{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg9viffdbeFDnzbsZEEW4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"When a handler panics with `http.ErrAbortHandler`, the recovery middleware now handles it the same way it handles a broken connection. It logs one short line instead of a stack trace, records the error with `c.Error`, and aborts. It no longer writes a 500. `http.ErrAbortHandler` is the standard-library value code panics with on purpose to stop a response (for example, the reverse proxy in `net/http/httputil` does this when copying the body fails), so it shouldn't be treated as a crash.\n\n**Changes:**\n- `recovery.go`: the panic value is checked with `errors.Is(e, http.ErrAbortHandler)` first, so wrapped versions are caught too, and then falls through to the existing broken-pipe check.\n- `recovery_test.go`: new test `TestPanicWithAbortHandler`. It checks that the status the handler already set (204) is kept, that the error is logged, and that the \"panic recovered\" stack-trace output doesn't appear.\n\n`gofmt` is clean and `go test ./...` passes.\n\nOne choice to flag: the middleware swallows the panic. It doesn't re-panic and pass it on to `net/http`. Because of that, a response that has already started isn't cut off mid-stream the way the standard library would do it; gin just stops running the remaining handlers. This matches how gin already treats broken pipes.\n\nThe changes aren't committed yet. If you want them committed, I'd use your title, `fix(recover): suppress http.ErrAbortHandler in recover`. You're on a detached HEAD, so I'd create a branch first."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1017,"cache_read_input_tokens":33306,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1017,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6f53edf7-3901-4754-b042-86c573750a1a","uuid":"eeb7f148-65b5-4f75-b477-871753ef6332","timestamp":"2026-10-18T15:19:11.946Z","request_id":"req_011Cg9vifSUgFfPZq2rRk9jf"}
